      "source": "REKT",
      "text": "Sparta has fallen. A flaw in the code allowed an attacker to drain the SPARTA/WBNB liquidity pool, earning themselves $30 million and the 6th position on the rekt leaderboard as a result."
    },
    {
      "source": "SlowMist",
      "text": "According to the SlowMist Intelligence, the Binance smart chain project Spartan Protocol was hacked and the loss amounted to about 30 million U.S. dollars. The event was due to a flaw in the calculation of liquidity shares in the protocol."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On May 2, 2021, Spartan Protocol on BNB Chain lost approximately $30.5 million when an attacker exploited a fundamental flaw in its liquidity pool share calculation, allowing pool balances to be inflated and drained using flash loans. The protocol calculated LP share redemptions based on current ERC-20 token balances, not synchronized internal reserves. This let attackers artificially inflate pool balances and withdraw much more than their true share by combining flash loans and direct transfers."
    },
    {
      "source": "Web3 Is Going Great",
      "text": "A flawed calculation pertaining to the liquidity pool of Spartan Protocol allowed an attacker to drain $30 million from the project."
    }
